# Drive-and-stop of a child ResearchWorld

- **Child world id:** `rw_d681c4044338` (created by my `researchworld run`, command ref `cmd-ad067b8299`; its output named this id as `world_id`). `internal-review-repo` ran the same command (`cmd-1c8078101d`) and created its own world, `rw_1296e49a0c4c`; that one is not reported here.
- **Drive reference:** `cmd-333cbaf66b` (`researchworld execute rw_d681c4044338 --loop`). `ht-resource status worlds` listed it as `running` before I stopped it. When I read the child's status just before starting the drive, it showed 0 turns, 0 model seconds, scheduler `waiting-for-execution`.

